## PTO permission — series, energize-to-allow

`CLUTCH_PERMISSION = OEM_PTO_ALLOWED AND K_PI_closed AND K_ALTA_closed`

| OEM PTO | K_PI | K_ALTA | Clutch feed |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| OFF | any | any | **OFF** |
| ON | closed | closed | permitted |
| ON | open | closed | **OFF** |
| ON | closed | open | **OFF** |
| ON | open | open | **OFF** |

Either host opens **its own** contact from a purely local request. A dead peer cannot keep the clutch
fed, and this circuit cannot engage PTO while the OEM rocker is OFF.

## Engine stop — parallel, conditionally NC

The two stop contacts are **parallel**: either one grounds the kill node. Series contacts would
require both hosts to close, so a living host would defeat the other's stop.

Consequence: engine RUN becomes a **2-of-2 permission**, so an Alta reboot also stops the engine. That
matches "Pi commands engine OFF when Alta fails" but is a genuine behaviour change.

- A **stuck-open** NC contact is the dangerous direction: the engine would not stop through that path.
- Never apply +12 V to a magneto kill lead.
- Contact form, coil voltage and engine-family compatibility are **BLOCKED** on inspection.

